---
# Reasoned suppressions for mobsfscan (make check-security-mobile). It scans a
# fresh prebuild of android/ and ios/ in a temporary directory, so every path
# below is relative to that prebuild. Each entry says why; an entry without a
# reason is not mergeable (docs/security.md, "Suppressing a finding, correctly").
#
# A malformed file is not ignored quietly: scripts/security/mobile.sh fails the
# run when mobsfscan warns that it could not read this configuration.
- ignore-paths:
    # The debug and debugOptimized source sets exist only in development
    # builds - they are how Metro's cleartext localhost connection works - and
    # are never part of a release variant. Scanning them reports cleartext
    # traffic the shipped app does not allow.
    - android/app/src/debug
    - android/app/src/debugOptimized
  ignore-rules:
    # StrandHogg 1.0 and 2.0 task hijacking on MainActivity. Expo generates
    # MainActivity with launchMode="singleTask", which expo-router's deep links
    # rely on. The mitigation (taskAffinity="" through a config plugin) is a
    # native change of its own and is tracked separately; until it lands this is
    # a known, accepted risk, recorded in docs/security.md "Accepted findings".
    - android_task_hijacking1
    - android_task_hijacking2
